+Use `--agent opencode --model <provider/model>` for OpenCode workers in the
+existing worktree. The installed Orca schema supports this with a verified host
+CLI and available model; OpenCode `--effort` is unsupported. For bounded R2 review
+use `--agent codex --model gpt-6.1-sol --effort high`; for the Astra route use
+`--agent codex --model gpt-6-astra --effort high`. Read the installed guide
+before launches. Verify requested/effective model and actual provider metadata;
+unsupported verification blocks launch rather than authorizing global rewrites.
+Keep one active writer per TASK and a separate context for its reviewer.
+
+Sol receives a bounded TASK/checklist, actual diff, evidence pack and previous
+findings; it returns a verdict and ends its turn. R1 diagnosis is allowed only
+at the escalation point defined by routing-and-budget.md, not as routine review.
+Do not automatically add a second Codex review after a valid Sol verdict. A
+necessary escalation preserves the logical TASK's counters and review slots.
+TASK-WINDOWS-PROGRAMDATA-01 remains on Astra for its existing R3/security review;
+this routing update neither resumes it nor allocates another review slot.
